e connection\"], \"produces_fact_ids\": [\"f-term-adopted\", \"f-known-leader\"], \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\"f-term-adopted\"], \"existing_protections\": [\"the fast path cannot append log entries, advance the commit index or run processLogs, because those fields are excluded by the heartbeat classification\"], \"cross_activity_effects\": {\"A7\": \"the fast path answers heartbeats without waiting for the main goroutine's disk IO, which is the documented purpose of the callback\"}, \"source_ids\": [\"s-raft-process-heartbeat\", \"s-net-fastpath\", \"s-net-handle-conn\", \"s-net-set-heartbeat\", \"s-api-fastpath-contract\", \"s-transport-interface\", \"s-integ-fastpath\", \"s-raft-append-term\", \"s-raft-append-leader\", \"s-raft-set-current-term\", \"s-state-term-atomic\"], \"unknowns\": [\"whether the connection goroutine and the main goroutine can interleave between the currentTerm read and the setCurrentTerm write on the same node in a legal history, and what term/leader value the node would then hold\"]},\n=== line 117 len 808\n    {\"id\": \"b-client-apply-verify\", \"primary_activity\": \"A7\", \"execution_owner\": \"client goroutines calling Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader; the leader main goroutine serves applyCh/verifyCh\", \"protocol_context\": \"client-facing contract of acting as leader\", \"trigger\": \"a client call on a node that may or may not be leader\", \"implementation_guards\": [\"a follower or candidate answers ErrNotLeader on applyCh/verifyCh/configurationChangeCh\", \"VerifyLeader steps down when a quorum does not answer\"], \"reads\": [\"raftState state/commitIndex\", \"leader identity\"], \"writes\": [\"responses on the futures\"], \"important_branches\": [\"a single-voter cluster answers VerifyLeader immediately\"], \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\"f-commit-index\", \"f-known-leader\"], \"source_ids\": [\"s-api-leaderwithid\", \"s-raft-leader-commit-consume\"]}\n=== line 131 len 252\n    {\"entry_point\": \"nested modules fuzzy/ and raft-compat/\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"reason\": \"These are separate Go modules with their own go.mod files and are outside the single module selected for execution.\", \"source_ids\": [\"s-raft-run-loop\"]}\n=== core_overview rationale ===\n\"Both core relationships and their connection are explained from actual code: formation and advancement are grounded in the vote tally, the pre-vote round, commitment.match/recalculate and the startIndex own-term rule; context and authority are grounded in the term/state update, leader identity update, the leader lease step-down and TimeoutNow. The connection is sourced: votes are only re-granted for the same term, older-term RPCs are ignored, match indexes are only usable at or after startIndex, and a transfer requires the target to be caught up. The one anomaly found while reading this backbone (the transport heartbeat callback that re-uses appendEntries from a connection goroutine) is recorded as a Behavior unknown and as the first Candidate rather than as a core gap, so the overview remains usable while that premise stays open.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
